>read it
This rutter is the record of your voyage from Rotterdam in the Netherlands 
south through the Atlantic, through the Pass of Magellan, up the west coast of 
South America, and into the unknown Pacific.

20
>write in it
You write: "April 21 1600. Fifth hour. Dusk. 133d day from Santa Maria Island, 
Chile, on the 32 degree North line of latitude. Sea still high and wind strong.
We are running before the wind along a course of 270 degrees, making way 
briskly. Large reefs were sighted at half the hour bearing North East by North 
half a league distant. Three men died in the night of the scurvy. Today Bosun 
Rijckloff died. I estimate we are still on course and that landfall in the 
Japans should be soon."

But how soon, you wonder?

