Time passes...



For three days and three nights, you fill your mind with facts and Japanese 
words and phrases. For three days and three nights you sit with Father Domingo 
and question and listen and learn and sleep in nightmare.

Then, on the fourth day, they call out your name.

"Anjin-san!"

"Thy confession, my son, say it quickly," cries Father Domingo.

"Go with God, Father" you reply, and the door slams behind you.

The air is incredibly cool and sweet, the clouds meandering before a fine 
southeasterly wind. You gulp deep draughts of the clean, glorious air. The joy 
of life fills you.

Prison Courtyard
This is a courtyard with great doors to the east. A line of naked prisoners 
stands before an official in a somber kimono.

You see Gray-uniformed samurai here.

