the ditch, Mariko translating with increasing amusement: "The pox on the karma,
the pox on the quake, the pox on the ditch -- I've lost my swords and the pox 
on that too!"

387
>inventory
You are empty-handed. You are wearing swords, a kimono, a pair of sandals and 
socks.

388
>give swords to Toranaga
You kneel in front of Toranaga and offer your sword as a sword should be 
offered. "Dozo, Toranaga-sama," you say. He accepts the sword and shoves it 
into his sash. "Domo, Anjin-san." He smiles, leans forward, and claps you once 
on the shoulder, hard. "Tomo, neh?" Friend, eh?

Toranaga rises, straddles the now narrow ditch, hitches up his kimono, and 
attempts to urinate into it. Nothing comes, and he laughs, inviting you to join
him.

325
389
>pee in fissure
Nothing comes, not even a dribble. You and Toranaga laugh at the sheer joy of 
being alive, which blocks you even more. At length you both succeed. You relax 
and collect your strength.

You lay full length on the ground and look up at the sky. A moment ago you were
all almost dead, and all worry and heartache was wasted. Karma, you understand 
karma now.
