Ochiba:
Reception Room
Score:345
Moves:431
Your feet take you under the final portcullis and your escorts lead you up to 
the huge door. Here they leave you alone. Desperate for any distraction from 
the ordeal to come, you admire the camellia blossom Mariko took from a vase in 
your quarters and gave to you. The flower is reassuring. Not everyone here in 
Osaka is an enemy.

You stand rigid for a moment, petrified with nervousness. What if you disgrace 
yourself? What if you slip or your swords fall or your limited Japanese fails 
you. You take a deep breath and walk forward into the flare-lit maw.

Reception Room
It is an immense, high-raftered room with a golden ornamented ceiling. 
Gold-paneled columns support the rafters, which are made of rare and polished 
woods. Five hundred samurai and their ladies are here, wearing all the colors 
of the rainbow. To one side is a line of guests who wait to bow before the 
raised platform at the far end.

On the platform, alone, is the Lady Ochiba.

Ishido, tall, lean and autocratic, stands beside the platform.

The procession of guests creeps forward, each politely bowing to Ochiba and 
greeting her on her birthday.

